    {
     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice: Dream Journal Setup",
     "content": "Practical exercise: Set up a dream journal tonight.\n\n1) Place notebook + pen at your bedside\n2) Before sleep, mentally state: 'I will remember my dreams tonight'\n3) Each morning, BEFORE opening your eyes, replay any dream imagery\n4) Write whatever you remember — fragments, feelings, colors, characters\n5) Date each entry\n\nAfter 14 days, review. Patterns will emerge: recurring themes, characters, emotions. Walker emphasizes the data trail reveals your emotional processing patterns.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Practice: Dream Journal</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#a0a0b0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">14-Day Setup</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#6366f1\" opacity=\"0.2\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"225\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Tonight's Setup</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"275\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\">Materials:</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"275\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Small notebook + pen at bedside</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"310\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">(or voice memo app if preferred)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"355\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\">Pre-sleep:</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"355\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">State intention 3 times</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"400\" width=\"940\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" opacity=\"0.3\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"435\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffd700\">Date</text><text x=\"280\" y=\"435\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffd700\">Dreams remembered</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"435\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffd700\">Themes</text><text x=\"860\" y=\"435\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffd700\">Mood</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"450\" width=\"940\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" opacity=\"0.1\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"480\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Day 1</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"490\" width=\"940\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" opacity=\"0.1\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"520\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Day 3</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"530\" width=\"940\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" opacity=\"0.1\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"560\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Day 7</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"570\" width=\"940\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" opacity=\"0.1\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Day 14</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"650\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#10b981\" opacity=\"0.2\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"695\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Review at Day 14</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"740\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• Did recall increase over time?</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"775\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• What characters recur?</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"810\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• Emotional themes (anxiety, joy, longing)?</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"930\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dream content reflects current emotional processing.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"980\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#a0a0b0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Increase in vivid dreams often signals improved REM quality.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Journaling reveals your REM emotional landscape."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice: 'Sleep on a Problem'",
     "content": "Walker's testable claim: Sleep on a problem.\n\nThe protocol:\n1) Identify a creative or analytical challenge (essay topic, design problem, code bug)\n2) Spend 15-30 min wrestling with it in the evening (loading the question into memory)\n3) Sleep a full 7-9 hours\n4) Return to the problem the NEXT morning — preferably with pen and paper at hand\n\nMany people report novel angles, solutions, or fresh framings. The associative REM has done overnight work on the problem.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Practice: Sleep on a Problem</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#a0a0b0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Engaging REM Creativity</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"170\" fill=\"#6366f1\" opacity=\"0.2\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"225\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffd700\">Step 1</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"225\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pick a problem</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Creative: essay opening, song hook, design concept</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"305\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Analytical: code bug, math puzzle, work decision</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"370\" width=\"940\" height=\"170\" fill=\"#10b981\" opacity=\"0.2\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"415\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffd700\">Step 2</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"415\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-weight=\"bold\">Load the question</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"460\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Spend 15-30 min on the problem in the evening</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"495\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Goal: encode it deeply so REM has material to work with</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"560\" width=\"940\" height=\"170\" fill=\"#ec4899\" opacity=\"0.2\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"605\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffd700\">Step 3</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"605\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sleep fully</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"650\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">7-9 hours with no REM-suppressing substances</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"685\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Late-night REM is when distant associations form</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"750\" width=\"940\" height=\"170\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" opacity=\"0.2\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"795\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffd700\">Step 4</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"795\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-weight=\"bold\">Return next morning</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"840\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Pen and paper ready. Re-engage problem before scrolling phone.</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"875\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Notes any new angles, intuitions, \"weird\" connections.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"970\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Track over 5 problems — note how many got fresh insight.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "REM works on what you give it to think about."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "What can dream content reveal, according to dream research?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "Specific predictions about future events",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "The current state of emotional processing — recurring themes signal active emotional work",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "Past lives or supernatural messages",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Random, meaningless brain noise with no relation to waking life",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Dream content is not predictive nor random. It reflects current emotional and cognitive processing. Recurring dreams signal incomplete processing of an issue. Stressful dreams often coincide with stressful periods. Dream characters tend to be people the brain has been thinking about. Walker emphasizes: dream content is a window into current emotional work, not prophecy.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Quick Check</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#a0a0b0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What Dreams Reflect</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"200\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#ec4899\" opacity=\"0.2\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ec4899\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dreams = Current Emotional Work</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\">Recurring themes:</text><text x=\"440\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Unprocessed issues</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"325\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\">Stress dreams:</text><text x=\"440\" y=\"325\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Active life stressors</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"360\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\">Recent characters:</text><text x=\"440\" y=\"360\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Recent waking attention</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"430\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#ef4444\" opacity=\"0.2\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"475\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ef4444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dreams Are NOT</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"520\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• Predictions of the future</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"555\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• Messages from supernatural sources</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"590\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• Random, meaningless noise</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"660\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#10b981\" opacity=\"0.2\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"705\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Walker's View</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"750\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">\"Dreams are an emotionally weighted, mostly visual narrative</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"785\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">constructed from current concerns and recent memories.\"</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"825\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffd700\">Pattern in dreams = pattern in life</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"950\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ec4899\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Journaling reveals YOUR emotional landscape.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Dreams reflect, not predict."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quote",
     "title": "Lesson 5 Synthesis",
     "content": "\"Dreaming provides a uniquely beneficial form of overnight therapy.\" — Matthew Walker. REM is not optional. It strips emotional charge from memories, links distant concepts into creative insights, and consolidates learning into integrated knowledge. PTSD is a failure of overnight therapy. Sleeping pills, alcohol, and cannabis suppress REM, blocking this work. Next: the health consequences of chronic sleep deprivation.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Lesson 5 Synthesis</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#a0a0b0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dreams Do Work</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"200\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#ec4899\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ec4899\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Function 1: Overnight Emotional Therapy</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• REM = only time noradrenaline is OFF</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"325\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• Memory replayed in calm chemistry</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"360\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• Charge stripped, fact preserved</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"395\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffd700\">• PTSD = stress chemistry stuck ON</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"420\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#6366f1\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"465\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#6366f1\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Function 2: Creative Integration</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"510\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• Links distant memories into novel associations</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"545\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• Bizarre dream logic = associative reach</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"580\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• Insights, solutions, inspiration</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"615\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffd700\">• Mendeleev, Kekulé, McCartney</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"640\" width=\"940\" height=\"160\" fill=\"#ffd700\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"685\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">\"Dreaming provides a uniquely beneficial</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"720\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">form of overnight therapy.\"</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"775\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#a0a0b0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">— Matthew Walker</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Lose REM = lose therapy + lose creativity</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"950\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ec4899\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Next: Sleep and physical health (heart, immune, metabolism).</text></svg>",
      "caption": "End of Lesson 5."
     }
    }
