     "explanation": "Spiegel et al.'s landmark studies showed: 4.5h sleep for 6 days produced leptin (satiety) drops, ghrelin (hunger) rises, glucose intolerance reaching pre-diabetic range, and ~300 extra calories per day consumption. fMRI showed amygdala hyper-reactivity to food and reduced prefrontal inhibitory control. This explains why sleep loss strongly predicts weight gain and type 2 diabetes.",
