     "explanation": "Hot bath dilates peripheral blood vessels (your hands and feet flush). When you exit, you lose heat rapidly through the skin, and your core temperature drops 1-2°F. Core temperature drop is a fundamental sleep onset cue — the SCN signals melatonin release when core temperature falls. Research shows pre-bed baths increase deep N3 sleep by ~10%.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Quick Check</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#a0a0b0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Why Hot Bath = Cool Core</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"200\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#6366f1\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#6366f1\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Step-by-Step Physiology</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\">1.</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Hot water → dilates peripheral vessels</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"325\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\">2.</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"325\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Hands and feet flush (radiator effect)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"360\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\">3.</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"360\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">On exiting, body sheds heat through skin</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"395\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\">4.</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"395\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Core temperature drops 1-2°F</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"430\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#ec4899\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"475\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ec4899\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Why That Helps</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"520\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• Core temperature drop = primary sleep onset cue</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"555\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• SCN signals melatonin when temp falls</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"590\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffd700\">• Deep N3 sleep boosted ~10%</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"660\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#10b981\" opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"705\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Protocol</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"750\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• Bath/shower: 10-15 min, hot but comfortable</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"785\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• Timing: 60-90 min before target sleep time</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"820\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\">• Then dim lights, cool room</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"950\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Heat outside → cool inside → sleep.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Thermoregulation drives sleep onset."
     }
